Theorem 1. With two arcs, the logarithm has a global branch on the circle.

Two arcs, each a little more than half of the circle.
They overlap in two pieces. The nerve records one.

Cover the circle by U1 and U2.
The transition on U1 and U2 is 1.

By gluing.

The value is 1.

WLOG.

The branches glue. Nothing leaks.
With two arcs the circle has no hole.

Now count both pieces of the overlap.

Cover the circle by U1 and U2.
The transition on U1 and U2 is 0.
The transition on U1 and U2 is 1.

By gluing.

The value is zero.

WLOG.

The hole is back. It was in the overlap.

QED.
